1
00:00:00,500 --> 00:00:06,980
The board sleeps for five seconds, wakes, blinks, reports, and sleeps again.

2
00:00:07,980 --> 00:00:13,222
Check the three drivers and paste both files. A sleeping chip may lose contact with

3
00:00:13,222 --> 00:00:16,380
the loading tool. Press Reset, or ask your leader.

4
00:00:17,380 --> 00:00:24,169
Line 86 is the low power timer. Line 87 is the wake up unit. Line 88 controls sleep

5
00:00:24,169 --> 00:00:24,660
modes.

6
00:00:25,660 --> 00:00:29,900
Switch on lines 128 to 141.

7
00:00:30,400 --> 00:00:38,080
Line 128: sleep five seconds. Line 129: the timer is wake source number zero.

8
00:00:38,580 --> 00:00:42,020
Line 131 counts wakes.

9
00:00:42,520 --> 00:00:52,280
Line 133 runs after waking. Line 135 asks whether the timer caused it.

10
00:00:52,780 --> 00:00:59,500
Lines 137 to 139 disable its interrupt, clear its flag, and stop it.

11
00:01:00,500 --> 00:01:03,940
Switch on lines 180 to 193.

12
00:01:04,440 --> 00:01:09,320
Line 184 loads default settings.

13
00:01:09,820 --> 00:01:18,780
Line 185 picks the slow clock, 1000 ticks a second. Line 186 counts it directly.

14
00:01:19,280 --> 00:01:25,360
Line 189 sets the period: 1000 times the seconds, minus one.

15
00:01:25,860 --> 00:01:31,380
Lines 191 and 192 let the timer wake the chip.

16
00:01:31,880 --> 00:01:33,880
For two seconds, what is the period number?

17
00:01:34,380 --> 00:01:39,380
Your turn. Pause the video.

18
00:01:39,380 --> 00:01:40,740
1999.

19
00:01:41,740 --> 00:01:45,580
Switch on lines 229 to 237.

20
00:01:46,080 --> 00:01:51,360
Lines 231 and 232 arm and start the timer.

21
00:01:51,860 --> 00:01:55,060
Line 234 prepares for sleep.

22
00:01:55,560 --> 00:02:01,240
Line 235 sleeps. This single line takes about five real seconds.

23
00:02:01,740 --> 00:02:05,100
Line 236 tidies up after waking.

24
00:02:06,100 --> 00:02:14,500
Switch on lines 270 to 277. They wake the board and print a banner.

25
00:02:15,500 --> 00:02:18,380
Switch on lines 310 to 318.

26
00:02:18,880 --> 00:02:23,360
Lines 310 to 314 make red an output, starting off.

27
00:02:23,860 --> 00:02:30,260
Line 316 unlocks the deep sleep modes. Line 318 sets the alarm.

28
00:02:31,260 --> 00:02:35,260
Switch on lines 352 to 361.

29
00:02:35,760 --> 00:02:41,760
Line 354 sleeps. Line 356 counts the wake.

30
00:02:42,260 --> 00:02:49,220
Line 358 flips the light. Line 360 prints the number and elapsed seconds.

31
00:02:50,220 --> 00:02:54,778
Build, load, press Reset, and time it with your phone. A new line should arrive

32
00:02:54,778 --> 00:02:56,220
about every five seconds.

33
00:02:57,220 --> 00:03:02,020
On line 128, try two seconds, then ten.

34
00:03:02,520 --> 00:03:07,896
With your leader, compare the current while asleep and awake. You now understand low

35
00:03:07,896 --> 00:03:09,560
power sleep, line by line.

